# Template for .env — copy to .env and fill in real values.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# .env is gitignored; this file is committed and must never contain a real
# credential. This repo is going to be public, so that distinction matters
# more here than it would in a private project.
#
# Per design spec Section 1.5, every path, connection string, and credential
# is supplied via environment, so the only difference between the macOS dev
# machine and the Linux production box is this file's contents.
#
# Sections are grouped by when the plan actually needs them. Anything marked
# for a later sprint is commented out — uncomment it on the day it is wired
# up, not before.


# ─── Generation mode (design spec Section 3.4.1) ─────────────────────────────
# local_only — generation happens only on local workers (DELL, MacBook). Paid
#              providers are never called, even if keys are set below.
# hybrid     — local workers stay primary; a configured paid provider becomes
#              the hedge partner for items at risk of missing a deadline.
# paid_only  — explicit opt-in. Local workers are bypassed for generation;
#              requests go to ElevenLabs, then Gemini Lyra 3.5. The filler
#              pool is still the last-resort fallback (Section 1.3).
#
# Left unset on purpose, so auto-detection governs: local_only while no
# provider key is configured, upgrading to hybrid as soon as one is. Adding a
# key below is therefore consent to spend money on hedging. To keep keys
# available for paid_only while refusing any automatic paid spend, uncomment
# this and set local_only explicitly — that is the documented opt-out.
#GENERATION_MODE=local_only


# ─── Sprint 1 / Day 1 — YouTube RTMP push ────────────────────────────────────
# From YouTube Studio → Create → Go Live → Stream settings.
# Use an UNLISTED test stream for all of Sprint 1; the real channel's key does
# not appear here until Day 18.
YOUTUBE_RTMP_URL=rtmp://a.rtmp.youtube.com/live2
YOUTUBE_STREAM_KEY=


# ─── Sprint 2 — DELL worker, Redis, NFS ──────────────────────────────────────
# Every worker - any OS - reaches the master over the regular home LAN/Wi-Fi
# (design spec Section 3.5, v0.4.2 revision). Workers run plain DHCP and
# self-register; only the master is fixed (OS-level static IP - see
# worker/setup.md).
# Day 4 wires these two up (Redis queue). Generate a real password with
# `openssl rand -hex 24`. The URL has no password embedded — workers read
# REDIS_PASSWORD separately so the secret never travels inside a URL.
REDIS_URL=redis://192.168.1.210:6379/0
REDIS_PASSWORD=change-me
#DELL_WORKER_URL=http://192.168.1.51:8001
# Day 6 wires this up: the worker's /health endpoint requires it in the
# x-worker-secret header. Generate a real one with `openssl rand -hex 16`.
WORKER_SHARED_SECRET=change-me
#TRACKS_DIR=/srv/radio/tracks


# ─── Sprint 3 — MacBook worker + Postgres (Day 8) ────────────────────────────
# The MacBook Air M4 runs ACE-Step natively (MLX) and claims jobs over
# Redis. Its address is not configured: it heartbeats on worker:macbook_air.
# Compose builds the in-network DATABASE_URL for playout and queue-manager.
# Generate a password with `openssl rand -hex 24`.
POSTGRES_USER=radio
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=change-me
POSTGRES_DB=radio
# Host directory mounted into playout at /srv/radio/tracks.
# On the Linux master set this to the NFS export: /srv/radio/tracks
#TRACKS_HOST_DIR=/srv/radio/tracks
# Day 9. How long a primary runs before the other local worker is
# started, and the backup's own window. 120 is the design-spec value:
# a bit longer than the MacBook's measured ~95s for a 30s clip. A
# shallow queue (deadline inside this margin) starts the backup after
# 1s. DELL publishes no heartbeat while parked, so it is not a partner.
#SAFETY_MARGIN_SEC=120
# Day 10 form. Open http://192.168.1.210:8080 on the master. Set
# INTAKE_BIND=192.168.1.210 to publish that port on the LAN address only.
#INTAKE_BIND=0.0.0.0
# Day 12 rate limit. One prompt per source per this many seconds (default
# 120 = one per 2 minutes). The source is the client IP, or an X-Client-Id
# request header when present (helps users behind one NAT). Uses the same
# Redis as the job queue; if Redis is unreachable the limiter fails OPEN
# (submissions still work) — it is abuse mitigation, not a safety gate.
#PROMPT_COOLDOWN_SEC=120


# ─── Sprint 4 — prompt moderation ────────────────────────────────────────────
# REQUIRED to accept prompts (Day 11). This moderates user-submitted text and
# runs before any generation source is chosen (Section 3.2). The `intake`
# service fails closed at startup if this is unset — the stream still runs with
# zero keys, but the prompt form will not accept submissions until this is set.
# Free, low-latency OpenAI moderation endpoint. It screens text only; it does
# not generate audio and is not billed per track.
OPENAI_API_KEY=
# Optional override if you proxy the moderation endpoint (default is OpenAI's).
#OPENAI_MODERATION_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1/moderations

# Optional second artist/copyright check — bring your own OpenAI-compatible
# chat/completions endpoint (OpenRouter, Together, Groq, a local llama.cpp
# server, etc.). The always-on keyword block runs regardless; this layers on
# top only when all three are set. Config-gated and mode-agnostic (Option X):
# when configured it runs in every generation mode. Leave unset to rely on the
# keyword block alone (and, in paid modes, the providers' own guards).
#COPYRIGHT_LLM_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/chat/completions
#COPYRIGHT_LLM_API_KEY=
#COPYRIGHT_LLM_MODEL=


# ─── Sprint 5 — optional paid providers ──────────────────────────────────────
# Genuinely optional. The app must start and run correctly in local_only mode
# with both of these unset; that is the single most important check in Sprint 5.
# Only ElevenLabs and Gemini Lyra 3.5 are supported — Stable Audio, Replicate,
# and Mubert were cut in spec v0.4 to limit maintenance surface.
#ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=
#GEMINI_API_KEY=
# Model overrides (Day 13 defaults shown). ElevenLabs: music_v2_5 is the
# current flagship. Gemini: lyria-3-clip-preview is a fixed 30s clip (our
# radio target); set lyria-3.5 for full-length songs.
#ELEVENLABS_MODEL=music_v2_5
#GEMINI_MODEL=lyria-3-clip-preview
# Optional seed for ElevenLabs' running credit balance, used by
# quota_remaining() until live usage tracking refines it. Integer credits.
#ELEVENLABS_CREDIT_BALANCE=
# Spend cap for Gemini Lyra 3.5, which is pay-as-you-go with no natural
# ceiling. Left unset deliberately — whether the repo should ship a
# conservative default cap is Open Question #7, still undecided.
#GEMINI_LYRA_SPEND_CAP_USD=
# If GENERATION_MODE=paid_only is set with NEITHER key above, the app fails
# loudly at startup (edge case #31) — paid_only has no local fallback.


# ─── Sprint 6 — YouTube Live Chat intake ─────────────────────────────────────
#YOUTUBE_DATA_API_KEY=
